<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banyo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banyo is a town in the Adamawa Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cameroon">Cameroon</a>, on the Adamawa plateau. Its Vute chiefdom was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> forces in the 19th century and became one of the lamidates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adamawa-emirate">Adamawa Emirate</a>, ruled by a lamido who paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yola">Yola</a>. It remains the seat of a traditional Fulani ruler.</p></div>
